# ─── Render (production monolith — API + UI on one service) ───
# Dashboard: New Web Service → build `npm install && npm run build`, start `npm start`, health `/api/health`
# Or: New Blueprint → repo includes render.yaml
#
# Copy from local .env into Render → Variables (no trailing slashes on URLs):
#   GEMINI_API_KEY, SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, PURGE_CRON_SECRET, DATA_RETENTION_DAYS
#   FRONTEND_ORIGIN=https://your-app.onrender.com,http://localhost:5173
#   LAZARUS_API_KEY=<same random string as VITE_LAZARUS_API_KEY below>
#   VITE_LAZARUS_API_KEY=<same value — baked into UI at build time on Render>
# Leave VITE_API_URL unset everywhere (UI uses same-origin /api; Vite proxies to :3001 in local dev).
#
# GitHub Actions purge cron: LAZARUS_API_URL=https://your-app.onrender.com (same PURGE_CRON_SECRET)

# ─── Local full stack (API + UI on this machine) ───
# Run: npm run dev
# GEMINI_API_KEY must be a valid AI Studio key (starts with AIzaSy)

GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY=your_assemblyai_api_key_here
# ASSEMBLYAI_SPEAKERS=2
# Universal-3.5 Pro (default) + Universal-2 language fallback — comma-separated override:
# ASSEMBLYAI_SPEECH_MODELS=universal-3-5-pro,universal-2
# Optional contextual prompt (U3.5 Pro). Avoid the word "speaker" — use speaker_labels instead.
# ASSEMBLYAI_PROMPT=B2B sales discovery call. Preserve filler words like um and uh.

SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_anon_key_here
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_service_role_key_here

# Data retention (days) — transcript_text nulled after this window; analysis_json kept
# DATA_RETENTION_DAYS=30
# PURGE_CRON_SECRET=random-secret-for-scheduled-purge-cron

# Production API auth — use the same value for both (generate a long random string)
# LAZARUS_API_KEY=your_production_api_key_here
# VITE_LAZARUS_API_KEY=your_production_api_key_here

PORT=3001

# FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173,https://your-app.onrender.com

# Windows TLS (if npm install or Gemini fetch fails):
# powershell -File scripts/export-windows-cas.ps1

# ─── Zoom RTMS (live meeting transcripts) ───
# Create a Zoom General App with Realtime Media Streams at https://marketplace.zoom.us/
# ZOOM_CLIENT_ID=your_zoom_client_id
# ZOOM_CLIENT_SECRET=your_zoom_client_secret
# ZOOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET_TOKEN=from_zoom_webhook_settings
# ZOOM_REDIRECT_URI=https://lazarus-4uxi.onrender.com/api/integrations/zoom/callback
# PUBLIC_API_URL=https://lazarus-4uxi.onrender.com
# Webhook URL: https://lazarus-4uxi.onrender.com/api/webhooks/zoom
# Subscribe to: meeting.rtms_started, meeting.rtms_stopped
# Also set ZM_RTMS_CLIENT / ZM_RTMS_SECRET (same as above) on Render for @zoom/rtms SDK

# ─── Google Meet / Workspace / Gmail ───
# docs/google-meet-setup.md
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Local demo (must also be listed under Authorized redirect URIs):
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3001/api/integrations/google/callback
# Production:
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://lazarus-4uxi.onrender.com/api/integrations/google/callback
#
# Enable Gmail API + add scope gmail.readonly on the OAuth consent screen.
# Existing connected users must reconnect once after enabling mail scopes.
# Add BOTH localhost and production redirect URIs on the Google OAuth client.

# ─── Microsoft Teams / Outlook (Entra ID / Graph) ───
# docs/teams-setup.md
# Add Microsoft Graph Mail.Read delegated permission; reconnect after changing scopes.
# TEAMS_CLIENT_ID=
# TEAMS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# TEAMS_TENANT_ID=common
# TEAMS_REDIRECT_URI=https://lazarus-4uxi.onrender.com/api/integrations/teams/callback

# ─── HubSpot (read-only OAuth — deal search + note import into Deal Profile) ───
# Create a HubSpot public OAuth app with ONLY these scopes:
#   oauth, crm.objects.deals.read, crm.objects.notes.read
# Redirect URL must match HUBSPOT_REDIRECT_URI exactly.
# Tokens stored in .data/hubspot-tokens.json (single-process; same pattern as Google/Teams).
# Optional webhook ingest (separate from OAuth): HUBSPOT_WEBHOOK_SECRET for POST /api/webhooks/hubspot
# HUBSPOT_CLIENT_ID=
# HUBSPOT_CLIENT_SECRET=
# HUBSPOT_REDIRECT_URI=https://lazarus-4uxi.onrender.com/api/integrations/hubspot/callback
# HUBSPOT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# OAUTH_STATE_SECRET=random-secret-shared-across-oauth-providers